      "writtenOn": "2018-10-08T08:56:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not without a ton of extra introspection. Instead of having separate methods called we now directly wire up routes to ensure we have the same code called in all cases. This means we would need to pull apart the request URI and know what request is deprecated and what is not.\n\nMostly the previous deprecation warning(s) were superfluous. It lets the operator know someone is using the old path. If the code is 100% identical, does it matter? The end user sees no information.\n\nWith v3 we are no longer removing APIs..",
      "parentUuid": "3f79a3b5_be3b6bc7",
